  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Round the middle player",
  "description": "Groups of three with one ball. The players stand in a line about 8–10 metres apart, one in the middle and one at each end.\n\nThe player with the ball at one end dribbles up and around the middle player – up one side and back down the other – and then passes to the player at the far end, who does the same the other way. Decide which way round to go: one time round the middle player, the next time round both the middle and the far end. Change the middle player about every other minute so everyone dribbles as much.\n\nVariants: the coach picks the foot (right only, left only, or inside and outside). Change direction, speed up or do a feint as you pass the middle player. Change the distance between the players. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep the ball close as you go round – lots of small touches."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use both feet and both the inside and outside of the foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up before you pass so your teammate is ready."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Speed up on the straight once you are round."
    }
  ],
